fcitx5-slm-ime (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The conversion runs inside the engine, in C++ (Eigen) on the CPU: no
    conversion server, no Java and no PyTorch. The slm-ime-server package is
    removed on the upgrade; the history of the user's choices stays.
  * The model is retrained on readings cleaned with KANJIDIC2, JMdict and
    Sudachi, and with the readings in hiragana as the user types them.
  * Key bindings: a key binding profile (Default, MS-IME, ATOK) and the keys of
    every operation, in fcitx5-configtool, with Japanese labels.
  * F6 to F10 put the active phrasal unit in hiragana, katakana, half-width
    katakana, full-width letters and letters.
  * Nothing is learned in password and sensitive fields; the history is
    readable by the user only; a damaged model file is refused.
  * Anthy is found as anthy or anthy-unicode.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0900

fcitx5-slm-ime (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The model is trained on FineWeb-2 (Japanese web pages) besides the Japanese
    Wikipedia: the character error rate on web text falls from 7.25 % to 4.89 %.
  * The candidates from Anthy are put in order by the model, after the text before
    the phrasal unit, and are fetched in the background.
  * The last characters of a long conversion are no longer cut off.
  * Without the text before the cursor from the application, the engine sends the
    text committed before; Ctrl+Shift+Insert takes the last commit back.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0900

